(text "OR2_N16: Y = A | B. One 6N16B (6Н16Б): two cathode followers with the cathodes tied (owner, 2026-10-28).\nPlates to +150 V; common cathode K -> Rs 2.2k || Cs 100p -> Y -> Rk 12k -> -50 V. The higher grid carries the current.\nInput: LV (1 = +10 V, 0 = -20 V), from its OWN divider on the driving HV net: 470k || C1 / 200k to -50 V,\nC1 = 2.7 pF per follower grid. Never share that divider with gate grids (NOT/NOR/NAND): they clamp a '1' at\n+0.4 V and Y then stays near -5 V. Output Y: LV, straight onto gate grids (no divider); fanout 10 grids.\nY must not drive another BUF_N16/OR2_N16 input or any HV input. Supplies: +150 V, -50 V, heater 6.3 V 0.4 A.\nSimulated, fanout 2/10 (input grid -5 V -> load plate 100 V): Y up 26/85 ns, Y down 41/241 ns. Ik 5.7 mA, Pa 0.74 W.\nHazard: A down with B up together dips Y; the load plate reaches 119 V at fanout 2 for < 0.2 us (73 V at fanout 10).\nPage: sch/logic/BUF_N16/README.md" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 177.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1e87c2b8-1c30-48a4-99d7-e352acc4447f"))

(embedded_fonts no))
